{"id": "EUVD-2026-81744", "enisaUuid": "d8f914c8-077b-3e72-9981-a063188cb43c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSv4: remove callback IDR entry on client allocation failure\n\nnfs4_alloc_client() allocates an NFSv4.0 callback identifier before it\nfinishes setting up the client. If any later initialization step fails,\nthe error path frees the nfs_client directly with nfs_free_client(). That\nbypasses nfs_put_client(), which is where the callback IDR entry is\nremoved during normal teardown.\n\nA failed allocation can therefore leave cb_ident_idr pointing at a freed\nnfs_client. A later NFSv4.0 callback lookup by cb_ident would find the\nstale pointer and take a reference to it.\n\nMake the callback IDR removal helper callable by the allocation failure\npath, and remove the callback identifier before freeing the client.\n\nThis was found by a local static-analysis checker for publish-before-free\nlifetime bugs and confirmed by manual inspection.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:50", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68c721391b761dbe38d5b0094d2bb6e8489ad92b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9bfdd0f591307b5198826a0e7a5b2f35f87acd2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c4812eb96bdcafb31a65b12f2aa96659429d1d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc95ca82d5ae598c428ab5a00ae69f8526d59371", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80b1c3d5a881f7d9081aa9f46da9742878a0f893", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f2387e8bfbc4efda5d77c3a11a028d0a119c48f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5891c03e150920618db0e9c4ea2d772abacdcfd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d05c2007b3d84ccba11dc6e9cb3202768cc72f14"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h72c-5c39-xm46", "CVE-2026-90151"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.74, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "053fb689-c1ff-30b3-beef-094a4392fd36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e36c33cbd2595eebcacb1 <68c721391b761dbe38d5b0094d2bb6e8489ad92b"}, {"id": "0568af60-587e-3076-9b4a-5857f948ef09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e36c33cbd2595eebcacb1 <5891c03e150920618db0e9c4ea2d772abacdcfd1"}, {"id": "39eeb290-8e45-3719-8423-6528cac660a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e36c33cbd2595eebcacb1 <fc95ca82d5ae598c428ab5a00ae69f8526d59371"}, {"id": "3c1e10b5-dd08-3b1c-8cb2-199b6cb19818", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "86f4ac55-41b4-3da2-a917-947fb104595c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e36c33cbd2595eebcacb1 <80b1c3d5a881f7d9081aa9f46da9742878a0f893"}, {"id": "89854041-97fe-350b-8e4a-23913e121960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "8fc386fe-dd6e-31e3-867a-abff3d4f2da1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "99f10598-1ea3-3629-a0ca-d1a28cb685f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "a23bd044-b70b-3edb-aef3-15b0cb9e32e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "a3c26de2-236a-3b5a-a64b-a1769860cd46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e36c33cbd2595eebcacb1 <7c4812eb96bdcafb31a65b12f2aa96659429d1d4"}, {"id": "a81a1650-aa5e-3b5c-96a6-50f834e178dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a8d9f6cf-5975-3f4b-8827-b8d8e1b884b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4eecd5da3422e82e88e3